      "id": "claim_c5b6828ef06a41998fe5e907fdb1618f",
      "statement": "Grounded Claims are material propositions that point to exact repository evidence such as `repo://src/server.ts#L40-L82` with the observed evidence version; the clean Markdown is kept separate from structured Claim state stored under `openwiki/.claims/`. On update the page worker submits only sparse Claim decisions (`confirmedClaimIds` / `claims` / `retractedClaimIds`), so issue-free Claims are retained automatically without being repeated through every model turn, while the complete current Claim set remains available through on-demand inspect. Claims currently apply only to repository code wikis, not connector-derived facts.",
