      "id": "claim_b9320b4df81b4ddaba8fe4f27d1dfa33",
      "statement": "OpenWiki can run inside a host coding agent (IBM Bob, Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode, Cursor, Kiro, Oh My Pi (`omp`), Antigravity CLI (`antigravity`), or GitHub Copilot CLI (`copilot`)) via a shared canonical skill and six MCP operations (`openwiki_begin`, `openwiki_submit_plan`, `openwiki_next_page`, optional on-demand `openwiki_inspect_page_claims`, `openwiki_submit_page`, `openwiki_finish`), where the host owns repository research, planning, and authoring while OpenWiki owns the durable queue, Claims reconciliation, source-drift handling, and deterministic finalization; the host submits only sparse Claim decisions per page and OpenWiki automatically retains issue-free Claims. Host-driven repository runs use repository source and tests only, not connector context. The personal wiki is served separately by an openwiki-personal MCP server and skill installed at user scope with `--personal`.",
